# `pluss::subsp::stats::ts::AcfOptions`

Options of `ts::acf`.

`AcfOptions` selects how many lags are computed, how the autocovariances are normalised and whether the mean is removed.

## Fields

| Field | Type | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `max_lag` | `std::int64_t` | 20 | The highest lag computed; the result has `max_lag + 1` entries, lag 0 first. A value larger than the series allows is clamped. |
| `norm` | `ts::AcfNorm` | `Biased` | `Biased` divides each autocovariance by `n` (a valid autocorrelation sequence); `Unbiased` divides by `n − k`. |
| `demean` | `bool` | true | Subtract the sample mean before computing; turn it off only for a series that already has mean zero. |

## Guidance

The defaults are a sensible starting point; change a field only for the reason its row gives.

